    "correct_option": null,
    "question_image": {
      "present": false,
      "description": null,
      "cloudinary_url": null,
      "latex_extracted": null,
      "source_page_number": null,
      "source_image_index": null,
      "ownership": "unknown"
    },
    "parts": [],
    "answer_text": "The Consumer Price Index (CPI) in India includes the following three components: 1. CPI for Industrial Workers. 2. CPI for Urban Non-manual Employees. 3. CPI for Agricultural Labourers. The rationale behind carrying out separate calculation of CPI is that the consumption patterns differ significantly among these groups.",
    "answer_latex": null,
    "steps": [],
    "final_answer": "Thus, separate CPIs are necessary to accurately reflect the impact of price changes on different consumer groups.",
